Task: In this task, you're expanding a game's item system. Implement the `Potion` class which inherits from `CollectibleItem`. Ensure the `Potion`'s `use` method correctly applies its effect to a target, but also includes a defensive check to prevent errors if the target is invalid or lacks the relevant stat.

Submitted code:
```
class CollectibleItem {
  constructor(name, rarity) {
    this.name = name;
    this.rarity = rarity;
  }

  describe() {
    return `This is a ${this.rarity} ${this.name}.`;
  }
}

class Potion extends CollectibleItem {
  constructor(name, rarity, effectPower, targetStat) {
    // 1. Initialize the parent class
    super(name, rarity);
    this.effectPower = effectPower;
    this.targetStat = targetStat;
  }

  use(target) {
    // 2. Defensive check for null/undefined
    if (!target) {
      return "Cannot use potion on an invalid target.";
    }

    // 3. Dynamic property check using 'in' operator
    // This is more robust than target[this.targetStat] as it handles falsey values (like 0)
    if (this.targetStat in target) {
      target[this.targetStat] += this.effectPower;
      return `Used ${this.name} on target for ${this.effectPower} ${this.targetStat}.`;
    }

    // 4. Handle valid target lacking the specific stat
    return `Target does not have ${this.targetStat} stat.`;
  }
}

// --- Usage ---
const healingPotion = new Potion("Healing Brew", "Rare", 25, "hp");
const player = { name: "Hero", hp: 100 };

console.log(healingPotion.use(player)); // Used Healing Brew on target for 25 hp.
console.log(player.hp);                // 125
console.log(healingPotion.use({}));     // Target does not have hp stat.
```

